<title>USA: USDA halts poultry imports from No.Ireland, Norway.</title>
<headline>USDA halts poultry imports from No.Ireland, Norway.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday it immediately halted imports of live birds and poultry products from Northern Ireland and Norway because of a recent outbreak of the exotic Newcastle disease in the two countries.</p>
<p>In a notice published in the Federal Register, USDA said it issued an interim emergency rule effective April 15.</p>
<p>The public can comment on the interim rule until June 17.</p>
<p>Exotic Newcastle disease is a contagious and infectious disease of birds. USDA said it would declare both countries free of the disease after one year of no reported cases.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk, 202-898-8467))</p>
